WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.707
On this slide, we are focusing on why dictionaries and sets matter.

00:00:03.707 --> 00:00:08.172
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.172 --> 00:00:16.407
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.407 --> 00:00:17.712
A set stores unique values.

00:00:17.712 --> 00:00:22.762
It is useful for distinct categories, membership tests, and comparing overlap between groups.

00:00:22.762 --> 00:00:25.122
Choose the structure based on meaning.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:30.392
Use dictionaries for labeled fields and sets for uniqueness or membership.

00:00:30.392 --> 00:00:35.407
A good data structure makes later code shorter and easier to reason about.

00:00:35.407 --> 00:00:41.167
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:41.167 --> 00:00:46.584
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
